    "body": "Looks already fixed on upstream/main a35c9cb81: repeated_adapter_probes_complete_without_a_native_abort passes without a change to production code. Suggest closing; the maintainer decides.\n\nThe temporary pin calls adapter_probe_names_the_gpu 16 times. It passes twice. The second run prints the llvmpipe Vulkan adapter on each call. It does not skip the probe.\n\nThe failed CI run exits with -1 without an assertion failure. Its log contains EGL permission warnings. These facts do not establish the cause.\n\nThe last green head is 5e76e6a14. The failed head is dee2bfcb5. Neither crates/ui nor xtask changed between these heads. I found no commit that proves a fix.\n\nThe pin does not reproduce the failure. Per the stop rule, I made no production change and opened no PR. The temporary pin is removed. Claim released.\n",
